                <pb facs="0737" n="725" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.515/8–944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-09T12:00:00+03:06">August 9,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 8:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>243. ReLegs 237, August 6, noon. To achieve a feature of stability in
                    riyal-sovereign rate during pilgrimage, the Saudi Government should offer to
                    convert sovereigns into riyals at a fixed rate. Jordan concurs in opinion that
                    such procedure is practicable and desirable. Such plan, which requires a
                    quantity of riyals in Saudi Government hands at beginning of pilgrimage season,
                    was effective last year though Government sales were small.</p>
                <p>Please advise what portion, if any, of 10 million subsidy riyals can be delivered
                    in Jidda by October 15. If the answer is “none” please investigate possibility
                    of obtaining riyals from those already minted for dollar riyal conversion scheme
                    and later replacement from subsidy riyals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
